IMPORT prelude

-- Superannuation (Pension Increases) Act 1971 (Cth). Source:
-- ../registers/source-bundle/C1971A00073.txt (compilation of 1 July 2014).
-- Seat: the pensioner, or the widow or widower.

§ `Nouns`

-- s 5(1), s 6: the pensioner's case for scaling.
DECLARE `Scaling case` IS ONE OF
    `no scaling`
    -- s 5(1)(a)-(e)
    `a case under section 5`
    -- s 6
    `a deferred pension`

-- s 8(1).
DECLARE `Spouse case` IS ONE OF
    `not a widow or widower`
    -- s 8(1)(c)
    `a widow whose husband elected that section 26 should not apply`
    -- s 8(1)(d)
    `any other widow or widower`

DECLARE `SPI 1971 case` HAS
    -- s 3 (for a widow or widower, the late spouse's figures)
    `adjusted unit entitlement`                         IS A NUMBER
    `actual unit entitlement`                           IS A NUMBER
    `scaling case`                                      IS A `Scaling case`
    -- s 5(2)-(3): the annual pension payable immediately before the
    -- commencing date, and what it would have been outside s 5
    `annual pension payable`                            IS A NUMBER
    `annual pension had section 5 not applied`          IS A NUMBER
    -- s 6: the units applicable under s 20(2) when the pensioner ceased to be
    -- a contributor, less any s 6(2) units
    `units when contributions ceased`                   IS A NUMBER
    -- s 7: increases under the 1957 Act s 11, the 1961 Act s 4, the 1963 Act
    -- s 26 and the 1967 Act s 4
    `earlier increases`                                 IS A NUMBER
    `spouse case`                                       IS A `Spouse case`
    -- s 9
    `an excluded pension`                               IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Rules`

-- s 4: $65 for each unit of the additional unit entitlement (the adjusted
-- over the actual unit entitlement).
@ref ss 3, 4
GIVEN p IS A `SPI 1971 case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 4 increase for` p MEANS
    IF p's `adjusted unit entitlement` GREATER THAN p's `actual unit entitlement`
    THEN 65 TIMES (p's `adjusted unit entitlement` MINUS p's `actual unit entitlement`)
    ELSE 0

-- s 5(2): scaled by the pension payable over the pension had s 5 not
-- applied. s 6(1): for a deferred pension, by the pension payable over $91
-- times the units applicable when contributions ceased.
@ref ss 5(2), 6(1)
GIVEN p IS A `SPI 1971 case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`after ss 5 and 6 for` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p's `scaling case`
    WHEN `no scaling` THEN `the s 4 increase for` p
    WHEN `a case under section 5` THEN
        IF p's `annual pension had section 5 not applied` GREATER THAN 0
        THEN `the s 4 increase for` p TIMES p's `annual pension payable` DIVIDED BY p's `annual pension had section 5 not applied`
        ELSE `the s 4 increase for` p
    WHEN `a deferred pension` THEN
        IF p's `units when contributions ceased` GREATER THAN 0
        THEN `the s 4 increase for` p TIMES p's `annual pension payable` DIVIDED BY (91 TIMES p's `units when contributions ceased`)
        ELSE `the s 4 increase for` p

-- s 7: "any increase ... under the preceding provisions" is reduced by the
-- earlier increases, not below nil.
@ref s 7
GIVEN p IS A `SPI 1971 case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the pensioner's increase for` p MEANS
    IF `after ss 5 and 6 for` p GREATER THAN p's `earlier increases`
    THEN `after ss 5 and 6 for` p MINUS p's `earlier increases`
    ELSE 0

@ref ss 4-9
@export default The increase in my annual pension under the Superannuation (Pension Increases) Act 1971 (Cth): $65 for each unit by which my adjusted unit entitlement exceeds my actual unit entitlement (s 4), scaled for the cases in s 5 and for a deferred pension (s 6), less earlier increases under the 1957, 1961, 1963 and 1967 Acts (s 7); for a widow or widower, one-half (if the husband elected out of s 26) or five-eighths of the late spouse's increase (s 8); nil for an excluded pension (s 9). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A `SPI 1971 case`  @desc The unit figures, the scaling case and its pension figures, earlier increases, the spouse's case, and whether excluded
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my 1971 pension increase for` p MEANS
    IF p's `an excluded pension` THEN 0
    ELSE
        CONSIDER p's `spouse case`
        WHEN `not a widow or widower` THEN `the pensioner's increase for` p
        WHEN `a widow whose husband elected that section 26 should not apply` THEN 1/2 TIMES `the pensioner's increase for` p
        WHEN `any other widow or widower` THEN 5/8 TIMES `the pensioner's increase for` p
